<title>MEXICO: Mexican jobs up 3.1 pct in first 4 months of 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexican jobs up 3.1 pct in first 4 months of 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The amount of permenantly insured Mexican workers rose 3.1 percent in the first four months of the year, or 282,782, from Dec. 31, the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) said on Friday.</p>
<p>The IMSS said in a statement the rise was the fastest in 20 years for the period, and compared with a 1.9 percent rise in the same four months of last year.</p>
<p>The total number of IMSS-affiliated workers was 9,446,241 at the end of April. In that month, 102,966 workers were added.</p>
<p>((-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
